[00:26.50] Thermal count is rising
[00:29.56] In perpetual writhing
[00:32.61] The primordial ooze
[00:35.88] And the sanity they lose
[00:39.34] Awakened in the morning
[00:42.18] To more air pollution warnings
[00:45.41] Still we sleepwalk off to work
[00:48.44] While our n-n-n-nervous systems jerk
[00:53.64] 
[01:04.92] Pretending not to notice
[01:07.81] How history had forebode us
[01:11.06] With the greenhouse in effect
[01:14.27] Our environment was wrecked
[01:17.95] Now I can only laugh
[01:20.31] As I read our epitaph
[01:24.07] We end our lives as moles
[01:27.02] In the dark of dawn patrol
[01:29.99] 